      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Single event",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( P(E)=\\dfrac{\\text{favourable}}{\\text{total}} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Complement",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( P(\\text{not }E)=1-P(E) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "AND (independent)",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( P(A\\cap B)=P(A)\\,P(B) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "OR (exclusive)",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( P(A\\cup B)=P(A)+P(B) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 8.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>A bag holds 3 red and 5 blue counters. One is drawn at random. Find \\( P(\\text{red}) \\).</p><p>There are \\( 3+5=8 \\) equally likely counters, 3 of them red:</p>\\[ P(\\text{red})=\\frac{3}{8}. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 8.B",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Find the mean of \\( 4,\\,8,\\,10,\\,6,\\,2 \\).</p>\\[ \\bar{x}=\\frac{4+8+10+6+2}{5}=\\frac{30}{5}=6. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Histograms (Frequency Density) <span class=\"tier-e\">E</span>",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "For grouped data with <em>unequal</em> class widths, plot <strong>frequency density</strong> on the \\(y\\)-axis, not frequency. \\(\\text{Frequency density}=\\dfrac{\\text{frequency}}{\\text{class width}}\\). Area of each bar equals the frequency for that class.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Frequency density",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(\\dfrac{\\text{frequency}}{\\text{class width}}\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Frequency from bar",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "area = class width × freq. density",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Cumulative freq.",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "Running total of frequencies",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "IQR from box plot",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\(Q_3-Q_1\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 8.C — Histogram",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>A class interval 20–30 has frequency 15; class width = 10.</p>\\[\\text{Freq. density}=\\frac{15}{10}=1.5.\\]<p>Conversely, a bar of height 2.4 over interval 30–45 (width 15) represents frequency \\(2.4\\times15=36\\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Conditional Probability &amp; Tree Diagrams <span class=\"tier-e\">E</span>",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<strong>Without replacement</strong>: after removing one item, the total decreases, so probabilities on the second branch change. <strong>Conditional probability</strong>: \\(P(A\\mid B)=\\dfrac{P(A\\cap B)}{P(B)}\\). Multiply along branches for \"and\"; add separate branches for \"or\".",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 8.D — Tree diagram without replacement",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>A bag has 5 red and 3 blue balls. Two balls are drawn without replacement. Find \\(P(\\text{both red})\\).</p>\\[P(\\text{both red})=\\frac{5}{8}\\times\\frac{4}{7}=\\frac{20}{56}=\\frac{5}{14}.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Using the same bag (5 red, 3 blue), find the probability of drawing exactly one red ball.",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(P(\\text{RB})+P(\\text{BR})=\\dfrac{5}{8}\\cdot\\dfrac{3}{7}+\\dfrac{3}{8}\\cdot\\dfrac{5}{7}=\\dfrac{15}{56}+\\dfrac{15}{56}=\\dfrac{30}{56}=\\dfrac{15}{28}\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "figure",
        "figure": {
          "type": "box_plot",
          "min": 15,
          "q1": 25,
          "med": 38,
          "q3": 52,
          "max": 70,
          "label": "Exam Marks Distribution"
        },
        "caption": {
          "en": "Box-and-whisker plot displaying the five-number summary: Min = 15, \\(Q_1 = 25\\), Median = 38, \\(Q_3 = 52\\), Max = 70, with interquartile range \\(\\text{IQR} = 27\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "warn",
        "label": {
          "en": "⚠️ Cambridge 0580 Traps — Statistics & Probability",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p><strong>Histogram Frequency Density:</strong> In Cambridge IGCSE histograms, class widths are usually unequal. The vertical axis is ALWAYS <strong>Frequency Density</strong>, where \\(\\text{Frequency Density} = \\frac{\\text{Frequency}}{\\text{Class Width}}\\). Frequency is given by the AREA of the bar, not its height!</p><p><strong>Probability Without Replacement:</strong> When selecting items without replacement, reduce both the numerator and the denominator for the second draw: \\(\\frac{4}{10} \\times \\frac{3}{9}\\). Forgetting to reduce the denominator to 9 is the classic exam error.</p><p><strong>Estimating the Mean from Grouped Data:</strong> Always use the <em>midpoint</em> of each class interval, multiply by frequency, sum \\(\\sum fx\\), and divide by total frequency \\(\\sum f\\) (never divide by the number of intervals).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "The table shows the time, \\(t\\) minutes, taken by 50 students to complete a homework task.<br>Intervals: \\(0 < t \\le 10\\) (freq: 8), \\(10 < t \\le 20\\) (freq: 14), \\(20 < t \\le 30\\) (freq: 18), \\(30 < t \\le 40\\) (freq: 10).<br>Calculate an estimate of the mean time taken.",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "<p><strong>Find class midpoints (\\(x\\)) and products (\\(fx\\)):</strong></p><ul><li>Midpoint 5: \\(8 \\times 5 = 40\\)</li><li>Midpoint 15: \\(14 \\times 15 = 210\\)</li><li>Midpoint 25: \\(18 \\times 25 = 450\\)</li><li>Midpoint 35: \\(10 \\times 35 = 350\\)</li></ul>\\[\\sum fx = 40 + 210 + 450 + 350 = 1050\\]\\[\\text{Estimated Mean} = \\frac{\\sum fx}{\\sum f} = \\frac{1050}{50} = 21\\text{ minutes}\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "[Probability &amp; Statistics · Practice 3] If the governing relation for this system is \\( g(t) = 5t + 5 \\), evaluate \\( g(8) \\) and find the inverse input \\( t \\) when \\( g(t) = 50 \\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "Substitute \\( t = 8 \\): \\( g(8) = 5(8) + 5 = \\mathbf{45} \\). Setting \\( 5t + 5 = 50 \\) gives \\( 5t = 45 \\implies t = \\mathbf{9} \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "[Probability &amp; Statistics · Practice 4] If the governing relation for this system is \\( g(t) = 6t + 6 \\), evaluate \\( g(10) \\) and find the inverse input \\( t \\) when \\( g(t) = 72 \\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "Substitute \\( t = 10 \\): \\( g(10) = 6(10) + 6 = \\mathbf{66} \\). Setting \\( 6t + 6 = 72 \\) gives \\( 6t = 66 \\implies t = \\mathbf{11} \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
